{
  "title": "Chronic Recurrent Multifocal Osteomyelitis (CRMO)",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pediatrics/4036/chronic-recurrent-multifocal-osteomyelitis-crmo",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 13 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Chronic Recurrent Multifocal Osteomyelitis (CRMO) is a condition characterized by idiopathic inflammatory disease of the skeleton that is associated with multiple sites of apparent osteomyelitis with negative cultures and no response to antibiotics.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is one of exclusion and can be suspected with multiple eccentric metaphyseal lesions with sclerosis and new bone formation, with negative culture and pathology results.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is usually symptomatic treatment with NSAIDS and pamidronate.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "incidence",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "1 in 250,000",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "prevalence",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "1 in 160,000",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "age",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "primarily occurs in children/adolescents",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "peak age of onset is **10 years old**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "male: female ratio",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**girls more common than boys**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Location",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "the tubular long bones and clavicle are most frequently affected",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "poorly understood",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Criteria",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**multiple sites of apparent osteomyelitis**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**pathology and cultures are negative**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**no response to antibiotics**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**Pustulosis palmoplantaris syndrome**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "a rare chronic relapsing condition causing **red patches and pustules on the soles of the feet and palms of the hands**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "considered a **rheumatologic condition** and no infectious agents have been identified",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "following the outbreak of the lesions, **desquamation occurs several days** later",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "associated with **CRMO**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**SAPHO Syndrome**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "CRMO associated with: synovitis, acne, pustulosis, hypersotosis, osteitis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "episodic fever",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "malaise",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "localized pain, swelling",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "focal tenderness in region of involvement",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Plain radiography",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "eccentric lytic metaphyseal lesions with surrounding sclerosis and new bone formation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4036/images/crmo_distal_tibias.jpg",
                      "caption": "Bilateral distal tibias with lesions consistent with CRMO"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Bone scan",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Can help determine other sites of disease",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "If concerned for malignancy, MRI can help determine presence or absence of soft tissue involvement",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Studies",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Laboratory values",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**WBC typically normal**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**ESR and CRP may be elevated**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Biopsy",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "biopsy and bone cultures negative",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "important to establish diagnosis which is one of exclusion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "symptomatic treatment with NSAIDS and pamidronate",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "treat during exacerbations",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "medications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "NSAIDs",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "corticosteroids",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "pamidronate can provide symptomatic improvement and stimulate vertebral remodeling",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Growth disturbance**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "rare but may occur",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Prognosis",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Natural history",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "characterized by periods of remission and exacerbation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "typically resolves in 3-5 years",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Prognosis",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "traditionally thought as having a relatively benign sequelae",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "several case reports of growth disturbance have been reported.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
